  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BRD - Socio-Economic Inclusion of Refugees &amp; Host Communities in Rwanda Project (SEIRHCRP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Refugees and host community  entrepreneurs in districts hosting refugees camps in Rwanda 
2. Refugees in Urban area specified in the project ToR
3. Business Development advisors in project area
4. Participating Financial institutions</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The SEIRHCRP objectives are to improve access to basic services and economic opportunities for refugees and host communities and support environmental management, in the target areas in Rwanda.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Socio-Economic Inclusion of Refugees &amp; Host Communities in Rwanda Project (SEIRHCRP) &#x201c;Jya Mbere&#x201d; is a Project financed by The International Development Association (World Bank) through an Agreement with the Republic of Rwanda. The Project financing amounts to US$80 million and is composed of US$35 Million of credit and of US$45 Million of grant.  


The project contributes to the ongoing shift from a humanitarian to a long-term, government-led developmental response to integrates refugees and host communities. 

 
The project adopts an area-based approach that supports refugees and host communities from the six districts that host refugee camps in Rwanda, namely Karongi, Gisagara, Nyamagabe, Kirehe, Gatsibo and Gicumbi. It targets also refugees1 located in urban areas of Kigali City (Nyarugenge, Gasabo and Kicukiro districts), Huye district and Bugesera district.  

 
The project is built on existing economic activities and opportunities for new employment in the target districts.</narrative>
  </description>
